course: dictionary
lesson: 2952
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Dad drives us to school» means he makes his car go and steers it. The clue is the school run, so drive means to take someone in a car.
explain: «In Bradford, Tariq's dad says no to a sleepover party, then drives Tariq there and picks him up at nine.» Ask: what would fit in the place of drives? Takes would fit, so drive means to take someone somewhere in a car.
explain: Drive can also be a noun. «A long drive to the beach» is a trip in a car, and «the car in the drive» means the short road from the street to the house. Read the words before and after the word to find its meaning.
explain: Drive can mean to push something along, like driving a nail, or a strong wish to do something. In computing, a drive stores files, so «save to the drive» means save to the storage part of the computer. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Drive is a verb and a noun: you drive a car, or you go for a drive.
fact: The past tense of drive is «drove», and the past participle is «driven».
fact: A «driveway» is the short road from the street to a house.
fact: In maths, distance = speed × time: a car going at 60 km an hour for 2 hours travels 120 km.
fact: Safety: wear a seatbelt, and children sit in the back. Drinking and driving is against the law and dangerous.
exercise: «Dad drives us to school every morning.» What does drives mean here? | *Takes us in a car | Stores us in a computer | Wishes for us very strongly | Pushes us along the road
exercise: «We went on a long drive to the beach.» What is a drive here? | A file saved on a computer | A strong wish | *A trip in a car | A nail pushed into wood
exercise: A car goes at 60 km an hour for 2 hours. Use distance = speed × time. How far does it go? | *120 km | 60 km | 30 km | 62 km
test: Which word is the past tense of drive? | *Drove | Driveway | Drives | Driving
test: «Save the photo to the drive.» What is the drive? | A strong wish to win | The short road to a house | A big bus with luggage space | *A part of a computer that stores files
exam: «Coach drivers are limited by law in how long they can drive without a break.» What does drive mean here? | To push something into place | To store files on a computer | To wish strongly to do something | *To make a vehicle go and steer it
